<Layout title="About" description="How Elsewhere checks Wi-Fi, power, laptop policies and access, and what each evidence state means."><article class="prose"><h1>Know what’s known.</h1><p>Elsewhere helps you find a place for a different workday in Dubai: cafés, co-working spaces, restaurants and hotel lounges. Instead of one overall rating, every amenity carries its own evidence, so you can see what was checked, when, and what still needs confirming.</p><h2>Reading the evidence</h2><p>Each amenity shows a value and an evidence state. The words carry the meaning; the mark and tone only reinforce it.</p><dl class="legend"><div><dt><span class="pill" data-tone="positive">Yes · Verified</span></dt><dd>Independently observed, with a source and date, within the last 90 days. The only state that passes a “Verified” filter.</dd></div><div><dt><span class="pill" data-tone="negative">No · Verified</span></dt><dd>Checked and absent.</dd></div><div><dt><span class="pill" data-tone="caution">Yes · Reported</span></dt><dd>A claim from the venue or a visitor that nobody has independently checked yet.</dd></div><div><dt><span class="pill" data-tone="caution">Yes · Needs recheck</span></dt><dd>A verification older than 90 days. It no longer counts as verified.</dd></div><div><dt><span class="pill" data-tone="caution">Conflicting reports</span></dt><dd>Sources disagree, so no positive claim is made until a new check settles it.</dd></div><div><dt><span class="pill" data-tone="unknown">Not checked</span></dt><dd>No reliable information yet.</dd></div></dl><p>Wi-Fi availability says nothing about speed. Work modes are our suggestions, not proof of amenities. Step-free access is recorded separately and is never judged from photographs. There is no venue-wide “verified” badge.</p><h2 id="reports">Reports from visitors</h2><p>Anyone can <a href="/submit/">submit a place</a> or report what they found at one. Reports start as Reported and only become Verified after an independent check.</p><h2>Your saved places</h2><p>Saved places stay in this browser. They do not sync across devices, and clearing browser data removes them. No account is needed.</p><h2 id="credits">Where the list comes from</h2><p>Places, Wi-Fi speeds, socket ratings and noise levels come from the Elsewhere list, built from our own visits and tips. Each one shows when it was added. Speeds and setups change, so anything older than 90 days needs a recheck. Places don’t have photos yet.</p></article></Layout>
